hub.com (ONLYOFFICE/server, Euro-Office/server).\\n')\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF"}}],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":32,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"PKT-0029 is only partly done: I could not find the upstream ONLYOFFICE commits for bugs 81132 and 81576. My permissions refused `git clone`, `gh api` and fetching github.com. The worktree has a single commit with no history and no upstream remote, so searching the git log finds nothing. I did not work around this, so the commit SHAs and diffs the goal asks for are still missing.\n\n**What I delivered instead:** an assessment based only on Euro-Office `main`, in `.theseus/diagnosis/PKT-0029-upstream-fixes-81132-81576.md`. It is marked as not checked against the upstream diffs.\n\n- **81132 (process crashes when a client disconnects mid-download):** `main` already has a helper that ignores client-abort errors (`utils.pipeHttpStreams`, `Common/sources/utils.js:982`), but only two places use it. The most likely crash point is `DocService/sources/routes/static.js:135`. If a client disconnects mid-download, its error handler tries to send a 400 after the response headers have already gone out. That throws, and nothing catches it. I recommend porting the fix, probably by cherry-picking it from the Euro-Office `release/v9.4.0` branch. The risk is low.\n- **81576 (shutdown hangs):** `DocService/sources/shutdown.js:73` waits until no document is left in the \"saving\" (SaveVersion) state, up to a timeout. If the final save fails and that state is never cleared, shutdown waits for the full timeout, which matches the bug. I did not find the code that should clear it. Recommendation: get the upstream diff before deciding. The risk is medium, because the change would touch save-status code that PKT-0028 found crash-prone.\n\n**Also done:**\n- Wrote a follow-up request in `.theseus/spawn/`: fetch both upstream diffs in a run that is allowed to clone from or query GitHub (`git clone` / `gh api` to github.com).\n- Filled in the Executor log and Lessons for the Atlas, and appended my friction line.\n- The packet declares no acceptance commands, so there was nothing to run. `theseus validate` reports 0 errors and 1 warning.\n- Committed as `ab3f8f4`.\n\n**Lessons for the Atlas:**\n- A packet that investigates upstream history needs network access or a local copy with full history, because packet worktrees have neither.\n- `utils.pipeHttpStreams` is the safe way to stream a file to an HTTP response.","ttft_ms":1764,"type":"result","duration_ms":80411,"uuid":"34401523-a076-4e71-8897-9059148bd14e","ttft_stream_ms":839,"time_to_request_ms":275,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":6,"system_prompt":136,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":3,"input_attachments":21,"input_hooks":3,"conversation_append":0,"transcript_persist":16,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":7,"init_frame_send":4,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":4,"message_prep":0,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":2,"request_announcements":14,"query_setup":4,"auto_mode_context_wait":7,"model_gates":1,"tool_schema_build":27,"message_normalization":2,"client_creation":6,"request_build":10},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":48,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":179,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"process_rss_mib_turn_start":218,"process_anon_mib_turn_start":143,"process_rss_mib_result":232,"process_anon_mib_result":139,"process_peak_rss_mib":262,"process_cpu_ms_turn":3447,"process_wall_ms_turn":80411,"process_cpu_ms_streaming":1787,"process_wall_ms_streaming":64984,"main_stream_count"